
🚀 Day 13 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 2965 – Find Missing and Repeated Values.

This problem helped me strengthen my understanding of Hashing and Mathematical Observation by combining a hash-based lookup with the sum formula to efficiently identify the repeated and missing values.

💡 Approach: Hash Set + Mathematical Formula

I traversed the matrix while storing every element in an unordered_set. If an element was already present in the set, I identified it as the repeated value.

Simultaneously, I calculated the actual sum of all elements. Using the expected sum of numbers from 1 to n², I derived the missing value using the relation:

Missing = Repeated + Expected Sum − Actual Sum

This allowed me to find both answers in a single traversal without extra nested searches.

